"""
Discrete-time F16 closed loop.

Sampled-data version of the continuous `ClosedLoopModel`: the continuous LQG
`BlockComponents.Continuous.StateSpace` controller is replaced with the pure-Dyad
clocked `DiscreteStateSpace`, fed with the ZOH-discretized controller matrices
(`DiscreteControllerA/B/C/D`) produced by `F16DiscreteLQGControllerAnalysis`
(disc="zoh", Ts=ControllerTs).

Every signal path is wired vector-to-vector. Vector arithmetic uses
`Utils.VectorConstant` (reference source) and `Utils.VectorAdd` (error, `k2=-1`);
the clock-crossing uses `MultiSampler` (continuous -> clocked, 12 ch) and
`MultiZeroOrderHold` (clocked -> continuous, 5 ch). The control-surface trim is
folded into the controller's output operating point (`y0 = trim_vals`), so the
strictly-proper controller emits the absolute control `u = C*x + trim` directly
and wires straight to the plant through the ZOH — no external feedforward add.
All blocks are templated like `MatrixGain` (structural channel count,
whole-vector equations), so no per-channel scalar wiring is needed.

Topology (mirrors ClosedLoopModel, vector-port plant `F16PlantModel`):
  ref.y --> err.u1;  f16plant.y_out --> err.u2           error = ref - measurement (12)
  err.y --> sample.u;  sample.y --> controller.u          continuous -> clocked (12)
  controller.y --> zoh.u;  zoh.y --> f16plant.u_in        clocked -> continuous (5)

The controller output already carries the trim via `y0`, so `controller.y` is the
absolute control command applied to the plant.

The 100 Hz `PeriodicClock` is planted on one controller input node
(`controller.u[1]`); the shared block clock propagates the sample rate across the
whole controller vector partition and to each per-channel Sampler/ZeroOrderHold
via clock inference.

Scenario: 10 deg initial pitch perturbation about the trim attitude.
"""
component F16DiscreteClosedLoop
  "Vector-I/O F16 plant; 10 deg initial pitch perturbation about trim."
  f16plant = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel(alt_init = 3000, theta_init = 0.17453292519943295) {^f16plant}
  "Discrete (ZOH) LQG controller as a clocked state-space block; trim folded into the output operating point y0."
  controller = DiscreteStateSpace(nx = 12, nu = 12, ny = 5, A = DiscreteControllerA, B = DiscreteControllerB, C = DiscreteControllerC, D = DiscreteControllerD, y0 = trim_vals) {^controller}
  "Controller sample clock (100 Hz), vector: one clock per controller input."
  clk = F16ModelWorkshop.VectorBlocks.VectorClock(n = 12, dt = ControllerTs) {^clk}
  "Reference set-points for the 12 measured states (vector source)."
  ref = F16ModelWorkshop.VectorBlocks.VectorConstant(n = 12, k = ref_vals) {^ref}
  "Tracking error block: error = ref - measurement (12 ch)."
  err = F16ModelWorkshop.VectorBlocks.VectorAdd(n = 12, k1 = 1, k2 = -1) {^err}
  "Vector sampler bridging continuous error -> clocked controller input (12 ch)."
  sample = F16ModelWorkshop.VectorBlocks.MultiSampler(n = 12) {^sample}
  "Vector zero-order hold bridging clocked controller output -> continuous control (5 ch)."
  zoh = F16ModelWorkshop.VectorBlocks.MultiZeroOrderHold(n = 5) {^zoh}
  "Reference values [npos, epos, alt, phi, theta, psi, vt, alpha, beta, P, Q, R] loaded from the trim TOML."
  structural parameter ref_vals::Real[12] = [F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.npos_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.epos_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.alt_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.phi_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.theta_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.psi_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.vt_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.alpha_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.beta_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.P_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.Q_init"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "plant.R_init")]
  "Trim control [T(N), el(deg), ail(deg), rud(deg), lef(deg)] loaded from the trim TOML; used as controller output operating point."
  structural parameter trim_vals::Real[5] = [F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "T_cmd.k"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "el_cmd.k"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "ail_cmd.k"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "rud_cmd.k"), F16ModelWorkshop.load_trim("trim/trim_point.toml", "lef_cmd.k")]
relations
  # Measurement -> error -> sampler -> clocked controller input (all vector-to-vector)
  connect(ref.y, err.u1) {^id10}
  connect(f16plant.y_out, err.u2) {^id11}
  connect(err.y, sample.u) {^id12}
  connect(sample.y, controller.u) {^id13}
  connect(controller.y, zoh.u) {^id18}
  connect(zoh.y, f16plant.u_in) {^id15}
  connect(clk.y, controller.u) {^id16}
